  "data": {
    "date": "2026-10-03",
    "definitions_and_caveats": [
      "Saved measurements from October 3, 2026; no new benchmark load was sent.",
      "Four-request bursts: sum of generated completion tokens divided by whole-burst wall time, including admission, prefill and decode. Three runs for TensorFold; one for SGLang. Dots are observed runs, not confidence intervals.",
      "Single-request decode estimates: one first call and one identical repeat per workload, each 512 output tokens. TensorFold repeats report 47/48 prompt tokens cached; SGLang cache accounting is unavailable. Runtime/cache state can affect results.",
      "Prompt latency is time to first token for uncached retrieval prompts of 8,205 / 32,782 / 122,892 actual tokens, labeled approximately 8K / 32K / 120K. One sample at each length.",
      "Configurations differ: SGLang uses its prior signed-W4 checkpoint, TensorFold its supported 4-bit checkpoint. Vision, slot count, KV dtype and prefill settings changed. These are configuration comparisons, not isolated causal engine or INT8 tests.",
      "The later two-slot baseline was copied from the earlier INT8 trial, not rerun immediately before the patched candidate. Original and later baseline sessions are shown separately to expose variability.",
      "Current four-slot preset passed four ~66K prompts plus 4096 generated tokens each, with all four simultaneously decoding above 64K context. Six active generations and four full 128K histories remain unqualified.",
      "Rejected stock four-slot INT8 trial omitted from deployed-stage plots: 388.08 / 396.57 / 395.41 t/s on short bursts, but failed long cache growth. Those rates are not a qualified alternative."
    ],
